{
  "version": 2,
  "reference": "Fresh Classic logical indices; no Native expected pixels or masks.",
  "rules": [
    "One set of floors per effect/scale applies to every mode and all eight seeds.",
    "Raw straight primitives have a 99.9% budget, backed by 4880 exact Classic-store line cases. Integer shift must be zero.",
    "Raw conic and filled-surface allowances cover only traced contour/older-ink and approved hole-fill differences, not a colour-phase offset.",
    "The 2x label doubles logical window dimensions: VGA400 Original fits 640x480 inside 640x800 (row pitch 1.2). Its intentionally broad phase envelope is paired with strict raw and 4K checks and a one-cell proximity guard.",
    "4K floors retain the measured sensitivity to nearest-centre phase at thin boundaries/crossings. Exact colour is measured only on shared ink; both ink overlap directions are guarded.",
    "These are regression budgets for classified variants, not universal mathematical accuracy claims. All metrics and raw/cyclic histograms remain reported; no differences are masked."
  ],
  "causes": {
    "arches": "Analytic ellipse versus midpoint contour; sample intervals count positions minus one. Midpoint colour cells replace tangent-dependent cap compensation.",
    "cones": "Separate analytic rings use exact original centres/radii. The conic boundary can overwrite different older rings than the midpoint contour. The original radius-1 circle includes the diagonal (1,1): its integer midpoint tie keeps Y unchanged. A true thin circle can miss that corner; the raw geometry budget is 1%.",
    "yarnball": "Original staged integer centres and derived radii; analytic/midpoint contour intersections can expose older ring colours. Sample cells eliminate the former -1 cap lag.",
    "gumballs": "Logical rectangular colour cells clipped to the analytic ellipse. At boundary cells the conic can replace an older ball that the cached raster left visible.",
    "daisies": "Original cached-ray pens plus the approved filled surface. Rays-only diagnostic is exact in shared raw ink; the surface fills moire holes and can cover older flowers through them.",
    "sine": "Join actual truncated/even original positions. Long steps fill unplotted cells, sometimes over older paths; the original point raster is sparse, especially EGA350.",
    "corkscrew": "Join actual truncated along/across combinations. Interpolated cells can replace older ink between the original isolated samples; reset breaks remain original.",
    "ellipse": "Original integer fan endpoints and midpoint colour cells. At reduced sizes a subpixel sample shift can select a neighbouring ray/colour band.",
    "littleStars": "Original manual sign/swap order and conditional copies. Reduced-grid phase can select a neighbouring ray with a distinct per-copy colour.",
    "bigstar": "Actual cached endpoints, including stale entries. Reduced-grid phase changes which crossing ray covers a pixel; no ideal-star replacement.",
    "boxes": "Exact raw logical-cell ray pens, with omitted terminal sample and separate reset origin. Reduction phase can select an adjacent fan ray.",
    "puffs": "Exact raw ray cells except incidental terminal stores. Sparse thin rays are sensitive to reduction phase, including diagonal nearest neighbours.",
    "bars": "Exact raw parallel segments. Reduced sampling can choose the adjacent shifted segment, normally one ramp index away.",
    "wandering": "Exact raw moving endpoints/segments; reduction phase changes coverage at crossings of differently coloured lines.",
    "squirals": "Exact original integer vertices and edge order, not pre-truncation vertices. Reduced-grid phase changes coverage at adjacent spiral edges.",
    "sweep2": "Exact cyclic ray cells; accelerating instances remain declared Faithful. Reduced sampling can choose an adjacent ray/colour.",
    "hexagon": "Original vertical/diagonal integer runs are exact raw and at 4K; 2x nearest-centre reduction changes coverage at short run endpoints with a 1.2-pixel VGA400 row pitch.",
    "hilbert": "The original line_step path paints overlapping square stamps at each point (width 1, 3 or 6). The Native width stroke partitions connected samples at midpoints, so a few stamp boundaries and per-point overwrite colours differ; 2x adds nearest-row phase changes. EGA XOR instances explicitly fall back.",
    "spiral": "The cardinal integer-step spiral is exact. The 2x preview keeps the same path and has no measured residual.",
    "spiral1": "The growing diamond increments colour before plotting the first point of each new circuit. Overlapping diagonal turn cells then differ by ramp index, with a few Native-only edge cells; 2x adds nearest-row phase changes.",
    "squares": "Cardinal integer circuits are exact raw and at 4K; a few cells at reduced circuit corners differ under 2x nearest-centre sampling.",
    "sweep": "The effect lengthens integer horizontal runs directly. At 2x nearest-centre reduction selects extra cells along long runs; raw and 4K are exact.",
    "zigstream": "Random integer runs and resets are exact raw and at 4K; the 2x row pitch changes coverage at short turns and resets."
  },
